<: if BRAND_KIND == 'business' :>1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,000
Every meeting you call needs
one line before it starts.

2
00:00:05,300 --> 00:00:09,500
Put the decision you need in
the first line of the invite.

3
00:00:09,600 --> 00:00:11,400
Not the topic, the decision.

4
00:00:11,900 --> 00:00:14,900
'Agree the price list',
not 'Pricing catch-up'.

5
00:00:15,300 --> 00:00:18,700
People arrive knowing what
they're there to decide.

6
00:00:18,800 --> 00:00:21,800
If you can't write it,
skip the meeting.

7
00:00:22,200 --> 00:00:23,700
Send an email instead.

8
00:00:24,300 --> 00:00:26,500
Try it on your next invite.

9
00:00:26,600 --> 00:00:29,600
Then come back
and tell us what changed.
<: elif BRAND_KIND == 'author-fiction' :>1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,600
Count the stones,
and the river lets you pass.

2
00:00:05,300 --> 00:00:07,200
Tam taught Maren the count.

3
00:00:07,300 --> 00:00:10,600
Three stones to the post,
four to the willow.

4
00:00:11,100 --> 00:00:14,800
Tonight she has to cross
the ford in the dark.

5
00:00:15,300 --> 00:00:17,200
She counts to the post.

6
00:00:17,800 --> 00:00:19,700
She counts to the willow.

7
00:00:20,700 --> 00:00:22,700
Then something upstream moves.

8
00:00:24,300 --> 00:00:26,900
That night is where
my novel begins.

9
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:29,200
Follow to see the cover first.
<: else :>1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,600
Making a newcomer welcome once
is the easy part.

2
00:00:05,300 --> 00:00:08,900
The real test of a welcome
is the second visit.

3
00:00:09,300 --> 00:00:11,400
Does anyone remember their name?

4
00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:14,800
Does anyone notice
that they came back at all?

5
00:00:15,300 --> 00:00:17,900
A welcome isn't finished
at the door.

6
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:20,700
It's finished when
they're expected back.

7
00:00:21,200 --> 00:00:23,100
That holds for any group.

8
00:00:24,300 --> 00:00:26,900
It's the heart of my next book.

9
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:29,600
Follow for the rest
of the argument.
<: endif :>